{"type":"thinking","text":"52 survivors, most are sprite/OAM. No obvious health byte. This strongly suggests health is NOT stored as a byte that changes between these snapshots in a simple way, OR my snapshot pairs (A0/B0/C0/D0) don't actually reflect health changes because... hmm.\n\nWait. Actually, maybe the heart display was NOT changing due to health at all! Let me reconsider: maybe the \"peach\" pixel is the heart blinking because Link is at full health and the game blinks hearts as a \"beep\" warning? No.\n\nHmm, actually, maybe the heart change I observed was caused by the game's \"damage invincibility\" flashing? No.\n\nHold on, let me reconsider: maybe the peach color is the heart's NORMAL appearance and the red is a \"flash\" when Link has full health? In Zelda, when you're at full health and have the sword, you can shoot sword beams. Not related.\n\nHmm. Actually, in Zelda, hearts are drawn as red hearts. When damaged, they empty. The empty heart is drawn as a white/peach outline. So my reading is right.\n\nBut maybe the game only updates the health variable at specific times (e.g., on the frame the damage occurs), and my snapshots captured the HUD shadow (0x0312) which changed, but the health variable might be somewhere that changed too. 0x0312 changed from 242 to 101 to 102. Wait — 101 and 102? The full heart tile is 242, and the empty is 102? But dD (B0→D0) had 0x0312: 242->102, and dJ (C0→D0) 101->102, dI (A0→C0) 242->101. So 0x0312 went 242 → 101 → 102. Two different \"empty-ish\" tiles (101, 102)? Hmm, maybe 101 = half heart tile, 102 = empty heart tile! And 242 = full heart.\n\nSo 0x0312 is the heart2 shadow? Wait, at 2 hearts, heart1 and heart2 full, heart3 empty. If 0x0312 is heart2's shadow, it should stay 242. But it changed to 101/102. So 0x0312 is heart3's shadow? Heart3 went full(242) → half(101?) → empty(102). Hmm, but the trace earlier wrote to 0x310 value 242. And get_tile_at_pixel(184,52) tile 242 at 2 hearts (heart2 full). So 0x310-0x312 might be the HUD row shadows for heart1,2,3.\n\nActually wait, dD said 0x0312 changed 242->102 between B0(full) and D0(2 hearts). If 0x0312 is heart3's shadow, that fits: full→empty, skipping the half? But between A0 and C0 (2.5 hearts), 0x312 went 242->101 (half). So 101 = half heart tile, 102 = empty heart tile. \n\nSo 0x0310, 0x0311, 0x0312 are the tile shadows for hearts 1,2,3 (or some mapping). These are OUTPUT (rendered tiles), written by the HUD routine from the health variable. Not the health variable itself.\n\nSo health is elsewhere and did NOT appear in dI/dJ. Why? Because health might not be a byte that changes value between A0/B0/C0/D0? That's impossible if hearts changed.\n\nUNLESS the health value is derived from a DIFFERENT variable that I'm not diffing because... hmm. Wait, diffs consider all 2048 bytes. If health changed, it must appear in dI (A0→C0 changed). dI had 58. Health must be one of those 58. And in dJ (C0→D0 changed from dI) had 52. Health must be in both (it changed both times). So health IS in the 52. Let me look harder.\n\nThe 52 non-obvious candidates:\n- 0x0004: 8->88 (and A0→C0: 88->8). So 0x0004 oscillates 88,8,88,85...? Actually A0=88, C0=8, D0=88. Weird.\n- 0x0005: A0=149,C0=6,D0=85.\n- 0x000D: 9->11->9\n- 0x000E: 9->11->9\n- 0x01F3: 12->136->12\n- 0x01F4: 126->125->126\n- 0x0312 (HUD)\n- 0x0341-0x0344: 34/26/160/252 → 14/6/120/196 → 34/26/160/252 (oscillates)\n- 0x0414: 0->1->0\n- 0x04F0: 0->5->0\n- 0x05F2: 0->122->38\n- 0x0610: 48->36->72\n- 0x061D: 3->7->3\n- 0x0670: 255->127->254\n\nHmm! Lots of these OSCILLATE (A0 value = D0 value, C0 different). That's a flashing animation (invincibility blink). The damage caused Link's sprite to blink, and these bytes toggle.\n\nWhich byte changed MONOTONICALLY with hearts? Looking: none obviously. \n\nHmm, wait: maybe health is stored as a value that changes only when the game \"commits\" it, and between A0 and C0 the health change is reflected... \n\nActually, hold on. Maybe the heart display is driven by a value that the game computes each frame and did NOT change monotonically because the \"2.5\" display was actually an intermediate animation. Let me reconsider: maybe when Link takes damage, the game plays a \"heart losing\" animation where the heart flashes between full/half/empty. So the byte 0x0312 (HUD shadow) cycled 242→101→102 as part of the animation, but the actual health variable is separate.\n\nBut the actual health variable must have decreased by 2 half-hearts. Let me look for a byte that decreased by exactly 2 between A0 and D0 and stayed put during... no wait, it would be in dD.\n\nHmm, in dD (B0→D0, from dA) the non-OAM candidates didn't include an obvious health. And in dI/dJ no obvious health. So maybe health is stored as a 16-bit value, or as a value with an offset, or as a bitmask.\n\nLet me look at 0x0670: A0=255, C0=127, D0=254. Changes 255→127→254. Weird, looks like a bit being toggled plus decrement. Hmm. 255 = 0b11111111, 127=0b01111111, 254=0b11111110. So bit7 cleared then bit0 cleared? Could be a \"blink mask\" for OAM.\n\nHmm. Let me look at 0x05F2: A0=0, C0=122, D0=38. Increases then decreases.\n\nHmm, 0x0610: 48,36,72. 0x061D: 3,7,3.\n\nNone monotonic over A0→C0→D0 except maybe 0x0312 (242→101→102) which is the tile.\n\nWait, maybe I mislabeled the heart states. Let me re-derive:\n- A0/B0: 3 full hearts (x=180,188,196 red).\n- C0: heart3 half (194 red, 196 peach).\n- D0: heart3 empty (194,196 peach).\n\nSo heart3 tile: full→half→empty. 0x0312: 242→101→102. So 242=full, 101=half, 102=empty. That's the tile shadow.\n\nSo some byte stores \"health in half-hearts\": full=6, C0=5, D0=4. Let me search for 6→5→4. Not found. What about full=3, C0=?, D0=? (2 hearts → maybe integer 2, and half flag separate).\n\nHmm, maybe health is stored as a 2-field: \"hearts\" (3→3→2?) no.\n\nLet me search for bytes with values 6,5,4 across A0,C0,D0. I can use diff \"equals\" 5 on C0 from dI? Hmm.\n\nActually, let me just READ the candidat