x6D08 runs every 2 frames (it's the HUD redraw). If it reads 0x066D, writing 9 should show. Unless the game overwrote 0x066D immediately.\n\nHmm, but 0x066D is the key/bomb count; the game wouldn't overwrite it each frame.\n\nWait, maybe my earlier test wrote to 0x660-0x66E and the HUD DID get the value but the display uses a different variable. Let me just test 0x066D directly: write 9, step several frames, screenshot.\n\nActually, hold on. Let me reconsider: in the trace of writes to 0x300-0x312, the routine at 0x6D08 wrote to 0x300-0x312. And the disassembly at 0x6D08 reads 0x066D and calls 0x6D50 with ldy #0x1b. So 0x6D50 likely writes tiles to 0x300+ based on the value at A (0x066D). So 0x066D is a counter.\n\nAlso reads 0x066F/0x0670 → 16-bit value → 0x6E79.\n\nAnd 0x0664 is a flag (maybe has-sword?).\n\nSo the counters are at 0x066D and 0x066F/0x0670. Hmm, but there should be THREE counters (rupees, keys, bombs). Let me read more of the routine: at 0x6D1A: ldx #2; lda 0x066D; ldy #0x1b; jsr 0x6D50. Then ldy #0x21; lda 0x0664; beq... Then more. Let me disassemble more.\n\nLet me disassemble 0x6D08 length 120.\n\nThen I'll see all the counters.\n\nLet me do it."}
